 * **Example**
 *
 * ```
 * const auto fit = dm::stats::welch_anova({1, 2, 4, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 3, 4, 5, 5}, {3, 5, 4});
 * std::print("{:.4f}\n", fit.statistic); // 4.1238
 * ```
 *
 * **References**
 *
 * - Welch (1951), On the Comparison of Several Mean Values, doi:10.2307/2332579.
 *
 * @param list<float> $values Finite observations concatenated by group.
 * @param list<int> $groupSizes At least two groups of size two or larger, each with positive variance.
 * @return HypothesisTestResult F statistic, numerator and denominator degrees of freedom, and upper-tail p-value.
 * @throws InvalidArgumentException C++ `std::invalid_argument`: Invalid sizes, nonfinite observations, zero variance or overflow.
 * @see one_way_anova()
 * @see games_howell()
 */
function welch_anova(array $values, array $groupSizes): HypothesisTestResult
{
    return \Datamunge\Rosetta\Runtime::call(195, [$values, $groupSizes]);
}

