 * Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: `$p = 0.5`, `$alternative = Alternative::TwoSided`, `$correct = true`, `$confLevel = 0.95`.
 *
 * @param int $successes Integer successes in [0,n].
 * @param int $n Positive independent-trial count.
 * @param float $p Finite null probability strictly in (0,1), default .5.
 * @param Alternative|int $alternative TwoSided (default), Less or Greater for true probability relative to p.
 * @param bool $correct True (default) applies the capped half-count correction to z.
 * @param float $confLevel Finite confidence level in (0,1), default .95.
 * @return HypothesisTestResult statistic=z^2, parameter1=1, estimate1=successes/n, p_value and uncorrected Wilson confidence bounds.
 * @throws InvalidArgumentException C++ `std::invalid_argument`: Invalid counts, null probability, alternative or confidence level.
 * @see HypothesisTestResult
 */
